tasks.prompt:
Here is a Python function in `solution.py`:

```python
def wrap(text, width):
    if width < 1:
        raise ValueError("width must be >= 1")
    lines = []
    cur = ""
    for w in text.split():
        if not cur:
            cur = w
        elif len(cur) + 1 + len(w) <= width:
            cur += " " + w
        else:
            lines.append(cur)
            cur = w
    if cur:
        lines.append(cur)
    return lines
```

Its specification: greedy word wrap. Words are maximal runs of non-whitespace (any whitespace — spaces, tabs, newlines, repeated — separates words). Lines are built greedily: a word is appended to the current line (joined by exactly one space) if the resulting line length is <= width, otherwise it starts a new line. A single word longer than `width` goes on its own line UNBROKEN. Returns the list of lines; text that is empty or only whitespace returns []. `width` < 1 raises ValueError.

Write a thorough test module `test_solution.py` using the standard-library `unittest` module that does `from solution import wrap` and tests this specification. Your tests will be run against this correct implementation (they must all pass) and against several subtly broken implementations (a good suite makes each broken version fail at least one test). Output only the test module in one code block.

